<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijaydurg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vijaydurg Fort, Gheria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijaydurg is a sea fort on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the mouth of the Waghotan river. Strengthened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> in the 17th century, it became a main base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> navy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanhoji-angre">Kanhoji Angre</a> and his successors and repelled attacks by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">English East India Company</a>, until it was taken by an English and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> force in 1756.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vijaydurg.jpg" alt="Vijaydurg" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ravi Vaidyanathan · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bastions_of_vijaydurg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Marathas also built an effective navy, with sea forts such as Sindhudurg and <b>Vijaydurg</b>, to defend the Konkan coast against the Portuguese and the Siddis of Janjira; under Kanhoji Angre in the early 18th century it challenged even the English and Dutch.</blockquote><a href="/empire/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
